---
import { BASKET_ITEMS } from "../../data/basketDefinition";
import { RAW_COUNTRIES } from "../../data/countries";
import { Badge } from "../ui/badge";
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardContent } from "../ui/card";
import Latex from "../ui/Latex.astro";
import {
  BookOpen,
  Scale,
  CheckCircle2,
  AlertTriangle,
  ExternalLink,
  HelpCircle,
  FileText,
  Sparkles,
  Home,
  Car,
  Stethoscope,
  Utensils,
  Calculator,
  Globe2,
  Layers,
  Activity,
} from "lucide-react";
---

<div class="flex flex-col gap-14 max-w-4xl mx-auto pb-20">
  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <Badge variant="outline" className="text-xs bg-primary/10 border-primary/20 text-primary gap-1">
        <Sparkles className="size-3.5" />
        <span>Scientific Whitepaper & Technical Documentation</span>
      </Badge>
      <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">• Open Econometric Methodology (2025 Standard)</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-foreground leading-tight">
      AtlasIndex Methodology, Mathematical Formulation & Living Standards
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      A transparent, empirical framework measuring genuine purchasing power across <strong>195 sovereign nations</strong> through standardized median wages, 13-item nutritional baskets, residential housing, private transport, healthcare diagnostics, and the <strong>Atlas Purchasing Power Index (APPI)</strong>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Table of Contents Quick Nav -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border/80 bg-card/60 p-5 backdrop-blur shadow-sm">
    <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
      <Layers className="size-4 text-primary" />
      <span>Table of Contents</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-2 text-xs">
      <a href="#macro-problem" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">1.</span> Conventional Metric Limits
      </a>
      <a href="#mathematical-models" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">2.</span> Mathematical Models & Equations
      </a>
      <a href="#appi-deep-dive" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">3.</span> What is APPI & Calculation
      </a>
      <a href="#non-food-pillars" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">4.</span> Housing, Car & Healthcare Rationale
      </a>
      <a href="#food-basket" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">5.</span> Nutritional Basket Composition
      </a>
      <a href="#data-sources" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">6.</span> Data Sources & Verification
      </a>
      <a href="#estimations" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">7.</span> Data-Sparse & Closed Economies
      </a>
      <a href="#limitations" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">8.</span> Caveats & Research Scope
      </a>
      <a href="#faq" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="text-primary font-mono font-bold">9.</span> Frequently Asked Questions
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 1: Executive Summary & Rationale -->
  <section id="macro-problem" class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-border/40 pt-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
      <Scale className="size-4" />
      <span>1. The Problem with Conventional Economic Metrics</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Why GDP per Capita & The Big Mac Index Fall Short</h2>
    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed flex flex-col gap-3">
      <p>
        Traditional macroeconomic comparative tools rely heavily on <strong>Gross Domestic Product (GDP) per capita</strong>. However, GDP per capita divides aggregate national output (including sovereign debt, corporate resource extraction, capital formation, and extreme top-percentile wealth) across the entire population. Consequently, GDP per capita obscures deep domestic income inequality. A nation with booming commodity export revenues can present an enviable GDP per capita of $40,000 while its median worker earns less than $400 per month and struggles to afford basic sustenance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Informal purchasing power parity indicators like <em>The Economist's Big Mac Index</em> attempt to quantify currency valuation through a single branded fast-food sandwich. While engaging, a Big Mac reflects multinational franchise royalties, brand positioning, proprietary supply chain contracts, and commercial inner-city rent overheads. It fails to reflect what actual working families consume: staple grains, cooking oil, fresh produce, dairy, protein, housing, and healthcare.
      </p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-4 text-foreground space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
          <Globe2 className="size-4 text-primary" />
          <span>The AtlasIndex Paradigm: Time as the Ultimate Currency</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
          Instead of measuring abstract monetary sums, AtlasIndex converts domestic consumer prices into the <strong>exact hours, minutes, and months of physical labor</strong> that a median-wage worker must perform in their home economy to afford essential human living pillars: basic nutrition, shelter, mobility, and preventive healthcare.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 2: Mathematical Formulation -->
  <section id="mathematical-models" class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-border/40 pt-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
      <BookOpen className="size-4" />
      <span>2. Core Mathematical Formulation</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Mathematical Models & Multi-Pillar Equations</h2>
    <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Every metric in AtlasIndex is derived from standardized mathematical equations using clean LaTeX formulation:
    </p>

    <!-- Formula Cards Grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
      <!-- Formula 1: Hourly Median Wage -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Calculator className="size-4 text-primary" />
            <span>1. Standard Hourly Median Wage (<Latex formula={String.raw`W_{\text{hourly}}`} />)</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`W_{\text{hourly}} = \frac{W_{\text{median}}}{H_{\text{month}}} = \frac{W_{\text{median}}}{160}`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            Where <Latex formula={String.raw`W_{\text{median}}`} /> is the national net take-home median monthly earnings from official labor surveys, standardized to <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{month}} = 160\text{ hours}`} /> (40 hours/week × 4 weeks).
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <!-- Formula 2: Monthly Basket Cost -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Utensils className="size-4 text-primary" />
            <span>2. Monthly Nutritional Basket Cost (<Latex formula={String.raw`B`} />)</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`B = \sum_{i=1}^{13} \left( p_i \times q_i \right)`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            Where <Latex formula={String.raw`p_i`} /> is the domestic retail price for item <Latex formula={String.raw`i`} /> and <Latex formula={String.raw`q_i`} /> is its reference monthly quantity in the standard 13-item adult nutritional baseline (~2,300 kcal/day).
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <!-- Formula 3: Food Basket Labor Hours & Wage Share -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Utensils className="size-4 text-primary" />
            <span>3. Food Labor Hours & Wage Burden</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex flex-col gap-2 justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{food}} = \frac{B}{W_{\text{hourly}}} = \left( \frac{B}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 160`} display={true} />
            <Latex formula={String.raw`\beta_{\text{food}} = \left( \frac{B}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 100\%`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{food}}`} /> gives the absolute monthly work hours required to purchase the basket, while <Latex formula={String.raw`\beta_{\text{food}}`} /> gives food cost as a share of the median paycheck.
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <!-- Formula 4: Housing Rent Labor Effort -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Home className="size-4 text-chart-2" />
            <span>4. Housing Rent Share & Labor Hours</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex flex-col gap-2 justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{rent}} = \frac{R_{\text{1BR}}}{W_{\text{hourly}}} = \left( \frac{R_{\text{1BR}}}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 160`} display={true} />
            <Latex formula={String.raw`\beta_{\text{rent}} = \left( \frac{R_{\text{1BR}}}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 100\%`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            Measures labor hours and income percentage required to rent a standard 1-bedroom residential apartment (<Latex formula={String.raw`R_{\text{1BR}}`} />) based on national median tenancy contracts.
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <!-- Formula 5: Vehicle Purchasing Power -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Car className="size-4 text-chart-4" />
            <span>5. Vehicle Purchasing Power (<Latex formula={String.raw`M_{\text{car}}`} />)</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex flex-col gap-2 justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`M_{\text{car}} = \frac{P_{\text{car}}}{W_{\text{median}}}`} display={true} />
            <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{car}} = M_{\text{car}} \times 160 = \frac{P_{\text{car}}}{W_{\text{hourly}}}`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            Represents the full months (<Latex formula={String.raw`M_{\text{car}}`} />) and work hours (<Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{car}}`} />) of median net income necessary to purchase a standard new compact passenger car (<Latex formula={String.raw`P_{\text{car}}`} />).
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <!-- Formula 6: Healthcare Diagnostic Checkup -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60">
        <CardHeader className="pb-2">
          <CardTitle className="text-sm font-bold flex items-center gap-2">
            <Stethoscope className="size-4 text-rose-500" />
            <span>6. Healthcare Checkup Effort (<Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{med}}`} />)</span>
          </CardTitle>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className="text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-muted/60 p-3 flex flex-col gap-2 justify-center items-center text-foreground font-semibold">
            <Latex formula={String.raw`H_{\text{med}} = \frac{C_{\text{checkup}}}{W_{\text{hourly}}} = \left( \frac{C_{\text{checkup}}}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 160`} display={true} />
            <Latex formula={String.raw`\beta_{\text{med}} = \left( \frac{C_{\text{checkup}}}{W_{\text{median}}} \right) \times 100\%`} display={true} />
          </div>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">
            Labor hours and income fraction needed to pay the uninsured outpatient tariff (<Latex formula={String.raw`C_{\text{checkup}}`} />) for a routine physician consultation and complete diagnostic lab panel.
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 3: In-Depth APPI Deep Dive -->
  <section id="appi-deep-dive" class="flex flex-col gap-5 border-t border-border/40 pt-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
      <Activity className="size-4" />
      <span>3. The Atlas Purchasing Power Index (APPI)</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">What is APPI and How is it Calculated?</h2>
    
    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed flex flex-col gap-4">
      <p>
        The <strong>Atlas Purchasing Power Index (APPI)</strong> is our flagship composite purchasing power metric, normalized on a continuous scale from <strong>1 to 100</strong>. A higher APPI score denotes superior economic resilience, higher real wages, and minimal labor strain required to satisfy baseline human nutritional needs.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-primary/30 bg-primary/5 p-6 backdrop-blur space-y-4">
        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-foreground flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>The Master APPI Formula</span>
        </h3>
        
        <div class="bg-background/80 rounded-xl p-4 border border-border/60 text-center">
          <Latex
            formula={String.raw`\text{APPI} = \text{clamp}\left( \text{round}\left( 0.70 \times F_{\text{wage}} + 0.30 \times F_{\text{hours}} \right),\, 1,\, 100 \right)`}
            display={true}
          />
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary block">Wage Burden Sub-Factor (<Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{wage}}`} />):</span>
            <Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{wage}} = \max\left( 0,\, 100 - (\beta_{\text{food}} \times 1.8) \right)`} display={true} />
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted-foreground">
              Evaluates the percentage of monthly median income consumed by food. The multiplier <Latex formula={String.raw`1.8`} /> scales a 55.5% food expenditure down to zero.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary block">Labor Hours Sub-Factor (<Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{hours}}`} />):</span>
            <Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{hours}} = \max\left( 0,\, 100 - (H_{\text{food}} \times 1.0) \right)`} display={true} />
            <p class="text-[11px] text-muted-foreground">
              Evaluates absolute monthly hours of physical labor. Scaled so that exceeding 100 hours of labor per month brings this factor to zero.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="text-xs text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-border/40">
          <strong class="text-foreground block mb-1">Why a 70% / 30% Blend?</strong>
          In microeconomic theory (specifically <em>Engel's Law</em>), the proportion of income spent on food is the single most accurate barometer of living standards. A 70% weight on <Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{wage}}`} /> reflects the household budget constraint. The 30% weight on <Latex formula={String.raw`F_{\text{hours}}`} /> incorporates the physical opportunity cost of human labor, penalizing economies where workers must dedicate unsustainable hours to stay nourished.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stress Tier Thresholds Table -->
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border/80 bg-card/60 p-5 mt-2">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-sm text-foreground mb-3">APPI Score & Nutritional Stress Classification</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
          <div class="rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 p-3 flex flex-col justify-between gap-2">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-emerald-500 mb-1">
                <span>Tier 1: Low Stress</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-500 border-emerald-500/30">APPI 75–100</Badge>
              </div>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">Food basket takes &lt;10% of wage (&lt;16 labor hours/mo). High disposable surplus.</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-semibold">e.g. Switzerland, USA, Denmark, Qatar</span>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 p-3 flex flex-col justify-between gap-2">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-amber-500 mb-1">
                <span>Tier 2: Moderate</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-500 border-amber-500/30">APPI 55–74</Badge>
              </div>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">Food takes 10%–20% of wage (16–32 labor hours/mo). Adequate access with moderate inflation sensitivity.</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-semibold">e.g. Poland, Chile, Portugal, Malaysia</span>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg bg-orange-500/10 border border-orange-500/20 p-3 flex flex-col justify-between gap-2">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-orange-500 mb-1">
                <span>Tier 3: High Stress</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-orange-500/20 text-orange-500 border-orange-500/30">APPI 30–54</Badge>
              </div>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">Food takes 20%–35% of wage (32–56 labor hours/mo). High household vulnerability.</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-orange-600 dark:text-orange-400 font-semibold">e.g. Brazil, South Africa, Turkey, Thailand</span>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-lg bg-rose-500/10 border border-rose-500/20 p-3 flex flex-col justify-between gap-2">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-rose-500 mb-1">
                <span>Tier 4: Severe</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-rose-500/20 text-rose-500 border-rose-500/30">APPI 1–29</Badge>
              </div>
              <span class="text-muted-foreground text-[11px]">Food takes &gt;35% of wage (&gt;56 labor hours/mo). Critical economic strain.</span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-[10px] text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 font-semibold">e.g. Nigeria, Pakistan, Egypt, Cuba</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 4: Non-Food Pillars (Housing, Car, Healthcare) In-Depth -->
  <section id="non-food-pillars" class="flex flex-col gap-5 border-t border-border/40 pt-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
      <Home className="size-4" />
      <span>4. In-Depth Rationale: Housing, Transport & Healthcare</span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Standardization, Decision Framework & Data Sources</h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Pillar A: Housing -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60 backdrop-blur p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div class="size-10 rounded-xl bg-chart-2/10 border border-chart-2/20 flex items-center justify-center text-chart-2 shrink-0">
            <Home className="size-5" />
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 w-full">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-foreground flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>Pillar 2: Residential Housing (1-Bedroom Apartment Rent)</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-chart-2/10 text-chart-2 border-chart-2/30">1 Month Contract</Badge>
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">National median monthly rent for a 1-bedroom self-contained dwelling</span>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Primary Data Sources:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li>National tenancy registries & census housing surveys (e.g. US Census ACS, Eurostat EU-SILC).</li>
                  <li>HUD Fair Market Rents, UK ONS Private Rental Market Statistics.</li>
                  <li>International urban rental audits & real estate registries (Numbeo, Global Property Guide).</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Methodological Decisions:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li><strong>Why 1-Bedroom?</strong> Represents the universal base unit of independent adult housing without roommate sharing distortions.</li>
                  <li><strong>National Weighted Average:</strong> We blend capital city, major urban, and provincial rentals weighted by population distribution rather than taking capital-city luxury penthouses.</li>
                  <li><strong>Exclusion of Variable Utilities:</strong> Utility bills (heating, electricity, broadband) vary drastically by seasonal latitude and are excluded to isolate the pure rental asset cost.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Card>

      <!-- Pillar B: Transport -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60 backdrop-blur p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div class="size-10 rounded-xl bg-chart-4/10 border border-chart-4/20 flex items-center justify-center text-chart-4 shrink-0">
            <Car className="size-5" />
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 w-full">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-foreground flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>Pillar 3: Private Transport (Standard Passenger Car Purchase)</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-chart-4/10 text-chart-4 border-chart-4/30">1 New Vehicle</Badge>
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Retail purchase price for a standard compact passenger vehicle</span>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Primary Data Sources:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li>Automobile Manufacturers Official Suggested Retail Prices (MSRP).</li>
                  <li>National Automobile Dealers Associations (e.g. NADA, Fenabrave, VDA).</li>
                  <li>National Ministry of Transport & Customs Tariff Schedules (OICA global database).</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Methodological Decisions:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li><strong>Standard Compact Benchmark:</strong> Standardized to C-segment entry compacts (Toyota Corolla 1.6/2.0L, Volkswagen Golf, Hyundai Elantra equivalent).</li>
                  <li><strong>Why New Purchase?</strong> Used vehicle markets suffer from unstandardized odometer wear, maintenance history, and disparate local lemon laws. New MSRP provides a clean, replicable benchmark.</li>
                  <li><strong>Full Fiscal Inclusion:</strong> Includes non-recoverable VAT/sales taxes, standard registration, and import tariffs (capturing major fiscal regimes like Singapore's COE, Brazil's IPI/ICMS, and Turkey's SCT).</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Card>

      <!-- Pillar C: Healthcare -->
      <Card className="border-border/80 bg-card/60 backdrop-blur p-5">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div class="size-10 rounded-xl bg-rose-500/10 border border-rose-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-rose-500 shrink-0">
            <Stethoscope className="size-5" />
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-3 w-full">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-foreground flex items-center justify-between">
                <span>Pillar 4: Preventive Healthcare (Routine Medical Checkup & Lab Exam)</span>
                <Badge variant="outline" className="text-[10px] bg-rose-500/10 text-rose-500 border-rose-500/30">1 Comprehensive Battery</Badge>
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Standardized clinical outpatient preventive consultation + diagnostic blood panels</span>
            </div>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs">
              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Primary Data Sources:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li>National Ministry of Health public/private medical fee schedule registries.</li>
                  <li>WHO Global Health Expenditure Database (GHED) & Out-of-Pocket Expenditure reports.</li>
                  <li>OECD Health at a Glance & private clinical diagnostic provider fee sheets.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>

              <div class="p-3 rounded-lg bg-background/50 border border-border/40 space-y-1">
                <strong class="text-foreground block">Methodological Decisions:</strong>
                <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-muted-foreground space-y-0.5 text-[11px]">
                  <li><strong>Standard Diagnostic Battery:</strong> Defined as: (1) General Practitioner clinical consultation, (2) Complete Blood Count (CBC/Hemogram), (3) Fasting Blood Glucose, (4) Lipid Profile (Total Cholesterol, HDL, LDL, Triglycerides), and (5) Basic Metabolic/Kidney Panel (Creatinine/Urea).</li>
                  <li><strong>Unsubsidized Out-of-Pocket Tariff:</strong> While nations with single-payer systems (e.g. UK NHS, Scandinavia) provide this near-free at point of delivery, we track the baseline unsubsidized fee tariff to reflect true diagnostic cost and evaluate out-of-pocket medical vulnerability.</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Section 5: Standard Food Basket Composition -->
  <section id="food-basket" class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-t border-border/40 pt-8">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
